# Project summary upkeep

- Read `PROJECT_SUMMARY.md` when starting substantive project work.
- After meaningful implementation changes, completed experiments, or agreed plan changes, update it in the same task.
- Keep it concise (approximately one page, no more than 700 words). Replace stale status instead of accumulating a chronological log.
- Keep the goal, delivered features, important results, limitations, and immediate next steps current. Link detailed observations and evidence.
- Distinguish live model results from synthetic tests, case accuracy from full-task success, and completed work from planned work. Never claim results for unrun experiments.
- Use America/New_York dates; distinguish the summary update date from experiment dates. Do not change historical evidence or scores when updating the summary.
- A summary update does not authorize additional experiments, API spending, or publishing.
